From 6a196210909adc1fede70d78b08e3b9045f42e63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/mux: make image sequence output work

The usage text says that images can be written by using '%d' in the
file name, but this failed with 'Could not open video codec': the
default encoder of the image2 muxer is MJPEG, which refuses limited
range YUV unless strict compliance is relaxed.

Mark the stream as full range for MJPEG. The generated picture uses
the whole range of sample values anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/mux.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/examples/mux.c b/doc/examples/mux.c
index a145eec..124f464 100644
--- a/doc/examples/mux.c
+++ b/doc/examples/mux.c
@@ -235,6 +235,11 @@ static void add_stream(OutputStream *ost, AVFormatContext *oc,
              * the motion of the chroma plane does not match the luma plane. */
             c->mb_decision = 2;
         }
+        if (c->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MJPEG) {
+            /* The MJPEG encoder only accepts full range YUV, which is what
+             * the generated picture uses anyway. */
+            c->color_range = AVCOL_RANGE_JPEG;
+        }
         break;
     }
 
